# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Local tooling (actionlint is downloaded by scripts/, never committed)
tools/

# Raw source archives. These are hundreds of MB and must never be committed.
# The FIRMS archives currently live a directory ABOVE the repo root, which git
# cannot see at any depth and is a stronger guarantee than this rule. This
# exists so that if anyone ever puts raw data inside the working tree, the
# ignore is already in place rather than added one commit too late. A 346 MB
# zip committed by accident cannot be removed from history without a force
# push, and the main ruleset blocks those.
raw/
*.zip
!fixtures/**/*.zip

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- vercel, keep as ONE block ---------------------------------------------
# `vercel link` appends its own .vercel and .env* lines to this file every
# time it runs, and it can write them with CRLF endings. Keeping these two
# entries together as a single commented block means a second `vercel link`
# produces a visible duplicate that is obvious in review, instead of
# silently stacking another copy somewhere else in the file.
# `.env.local` holds a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN. It must never be committed.
# See ARCHITECTURE.md section 8.
.vercel
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# --- end vercel block ------------------------------------------------------

# `vercel link` appends its own duplicate `.vercel` and `.env*` lines below
# this point, with CRLF endings, every time it runs. Observed on 2026-11-06.
# They are removed deliberately: the block above already covers both, and a
# bare `.env*` placed after the `!.env.example` negation would silently
# re-ignore the example file. If you see duplicates here, a `vercel link` has
# run; delete them rather than leaving two sources of truth.
